body:
Hi, I'm trying to run this code with mssql:

```ts
import sql from "npm:mssql@10.0.1";

const sqlConfig = {
  server: "localhost",
  user: "sa",
  password: "",
  database: "my_db",
  options: {
    trustServerCertificate: true,
  },
};

const pool = await sql.connect(sqlConfig);
const result = await pool.request().execute("spGetPurchases");

console.dir(result);

```

But I get `Uncaught (in promise) ConnectionError: Failed to connect to localhost:1433 in 15000ms`

![image](https://github.com/denoland/deno/assets/7959437/0b985b64-7653-4c06-b3c0-5d934d066aa5)

I decided to do the same with Node v18.16.0 and worked perfectly:

```js
const sql = require("mssql");

const sqlConfig = {
  server: "localhost",
  user: "sa",
  password: "",
  database: "my_db",
  options: {
    trustServerCertificate: true,
  },
};

(async () => {
  const pool = await sql.connect(sqlConfig);
  const result2 = await pool.request().execute("spGetPurchases");

  console.dir(result2);
})();

```
![image](https://github.com/denoland/deno/assets/7959437/bb59e95f-6844-46d1-b6e2-77fe60b68c27)

The SQL Server is running inside a Docker container:

![image](https://github.com/denoland/deno/assets/7959437/5e4d5034-b748-4bff-8a5d-5ea6c23c663a)

I'm using Deno latest version as of today v1.37.0

